ck-mckim","vote":"no"},{"name":"Nita Green","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10950","person_slug":"nita-green","vote":"no"},{"name":"Paul Scarr","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10949","person_slug":"paul-scarr","vote":"no"},{"name":"Pauline Hanson","party":"One Nation","person_id":"tvfy_10280","person_slug":"pauline-hanson","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Penny Allman-Payne","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_11002","person_slug":"penny-allman-payne","vote":"no"},{"name":"Peter Whish-Wilson","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10780","person_slug":"peter-whish-wilson","vote":"no"},{"name":"Raff Ciccone","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10915","person_slug":"raff-ciccone","vote":"no"},{"name":"Ralph Babet","party":"United Australia Party","person_id":"tvfy_11003","person_slug":"ralph-babet","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Richard Dowling","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_11056","person_slug":"richard-dowling","vote":"no"},{"name":"Sarah Hanson-Young","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10711","person_slug":"sarah-hanson-young","vote":"no"},{"name":"Slade Brockman","party":"DPRES","person_id":"tvfy_10900","person_slug":"slade-brockman","vote":"no"},{"name":"Steph Hodgins-May","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_11020","person_slug":"steph-hodgins-may","vote":"no"},{"name":"Tammy Tyrrell","party":"Independent","person_id":"tvfy_11012","person_slug":"tammy-tyrrell","vote":"no"},{"name":"Tim Ayres","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10946","person_slug":"tim-ayres","vote":"no"},{"name":"Tony Sheldon","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10944","person_slug":"tony-sheldon","vote":"no"},{"name":"Tyron Whitten","party":"One Nation","person_id":"tvfy_11060","person_slug":"tyron-whitten","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Varun Ghosh","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_11017","person_slug":"varun-ghosh","vote":"no"},{"name":"Warwick Stacey","party":"One Nation","person_id":"tvfy_11061","person_slug":"warwick-stacey","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Wendy Askew","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10914","person_slug":"wendy-askew","vote":"no"}],"name":"Health Legislation Amendment (Improved Medicare Integrity and Other Measures) Bill 2025 - in Committee - Therapeutic goods approvals to be by legislative instrument","noes":45,"question":"The majority voted against an [amendment (1) on sheet 3379](https://www.openaustralia.org.au/senate/?gid=2025-07-28.54.1), moved by Queensland Senator [Malcolm Roberts](https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/people/senate/queensland/malcolm_roberts) (One Nation), which means it failed. ### Amendment text > *(1) Schedule 2, Part 6, page 22 (line 1) to page 23 (line 22), omit the Part, substitute:* > > *Part 6 — Therapeutic goods approvals* > > *Therapeutic Goods Act 1989* > > *52 Subsection 19(1)* > >> *Repeal the subsection, substitute:* >> >> *(1) The Secretary may, by legislative instrument, grant an approval to a person for the importation into, or the exportation from, Australia or the supply in Australia of specified therapeutic goods that are not registered goods or listed goods:* >> >>> *(a) for use in the treatment of another person; or* >>> >>> *(b) for use solely for experimental purposes in humans;* >>> >>> *and such an approval may be given subject to such conditions as are specified in the instrument.* >>> >>> *Note: For variation of an approval for use of the kind referred to in paragraph (1)(b), see subsection (4B).* >> >> *(1AAA) A legislative instrument made under subsection (1) must set out the reasons for the approval.* > > *53 Subsection 19(4B)* > >> *Omit \"by notice in writing\", substitute \"by legislative instrument\".*","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-senate-9641","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2025-07-28/3"}
